 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "The transformation (166) is never drawn; glossed only «قولا قدريا… وأبعدهم اللّه من رحمته». 167:4-12 is glossed «يهينهم، ويذلهم» without naming any present-day people. Their claim «سيغفر لنا» is framed «تمنيًا على الله الأباطيل». First-person «قطعناهم… بلوناهم» not used; As-Sa'di's «خير وأبقى» avoided. 169: short-word flag, listen. STAGING v4: c1 (166-167) stays ambient (night sky): 166 is the decree on the Sabbath-breakers and 167 the humiliation sent upon them until the Day; no ape, no transformation, no punished person and no afflicter is drawn, only camera moves through 166; an hourglass for 167:6-12 (until the Day), a geometric plate from 167:13 to the end over the Lord's swift penalty and His forgiveness (no light plate on the attribute or the pronoun at 167:17-18). c2 (168-169) is a stage in a town by day: two groups apart for 168:1-4 (dispersed into communities), the camera on the righteous (believers, left, 168:6) and on the others (people, right, 168:8); a night-and-day plate for the test with ease and hardship (168:10); no gesture on the hoped-for return (168:13). 169: the others leave as the verse turns to the generation after them (169:1) and three men enter at the centre (169:3, the successors; three because the tafsirs describe men who give rulings); they hold the Book (169:6, they inherited it) and a rich man who came in at 169:6 hands them a purse on 169:7 (taking the goods of this world: Al-Muyassar names bribery, As-Sa'di says money was given to them to rule unjustly and bribery spread; the giver is only the one who pays, no person is meant); a coins plate for the worldly goods (169:8-10); they speak their claim on 169:11 (framed by the gloss as wishful thinking); the conditional 169:14-18 gets camera only; the rich man leaves at 169:19; a seal plate for the covenant of the Book over 169:22-30 (the Name at 169:28 under a seal); they read again on 169:31 (they studied what is in it); a light plate for the abode of the Hereafter (169:34-38, a symbol, nothing literal), the camera on the believers who bow in humility on 169:38 (those who fear Allah) and back on the successors for 169:39-40. FOR THE REVIEWER: the bribe-giver is a generic rich man implied by both tafsirs' bribery; he is not in the verse wording."
 },
